# -Indexes, not +Indexes: with listings on, any directory without an index file
# is browsable, so GET /gpt/docker/ (or /gpt/backend/src/... anywhere the
# subdirectory has no .htaccess of its own) returns a full file listing. This
# file sits at the app root and AllowOverride lets it win over the vhost, so
# +Indexes here re-enabled listings even where a parent config had denied them.
# DirectoryIndex below still serves index.html/index.php normally.
Options -Indexes +FollowSymLinks
DirectoryIndex index.html index.php
<IfModule mod_headers.c>
    Header set Access-Control-Allow-Origin "*"
</IfModule>
